1. Product vision and core rules
Familiar video experience

A searchable homepage, video feeds, creator channels, recommendations, categories, comments and a powerful player.



Pay-per-video purchasing

Every paid video has a price. Users can preview it, purchase it and access it from their personal library.



Verified access

Only a confirmed, valid purchase grants paid playback. Frontend buttons never determine whether a video has been paid for.



Transparent creator earnings

PayTune calculates its commission, creator earnings, refunds, settlements and payout records for every transaction.



Non-negotiable business rules
- One successful purchase grants the user unlimited streaming access to that video without a second charge.
- A duplicate payment notification must never create a duplicate purchase or creator earning.
- A failed, cancelled or unverified payment must not unlock playback.
- Videos can be uploaded only by administrators or approved creators.
- Creators can manage their own videos, but cannot change purchase records, commissions or payment status.
- Administrators can moderate content, manage accounts and investigate transactions through an audit trail.
- “Forever” means no recurring charge or routine expiration of the purchased entitlement. It cannot guarantee availability if legal restrictions, copyright disputes, or platform closure intervene. Those cases need an explicit policy.
2. User roles and permission system
PayTune should have four main roles. A single account may be a viewer and an approved creator, but administrator privileges must remain separate and tightly controlled.

1. Viewer

Discover and preview content, buy videos, watch purchased content, save favorites, follow creators, comment, rate, report abuse and manage purchases.




2. Approved creator

Upload videos, set prices, manage publishing, view analytics, track sales, submit payout details, view earnings and respond to comments.

New applicants cannot sell paid videos until an administrator approves their creator application.




3. Administrator

Approve creators, moderate videos, investigate reports, manage users, configure commissions, review transactions and oversee payouts.




4. Super administrator

Manage administrators, system-wide settings, security policies, payment-provider configuration and high-risk financial operations.



Permission rules
- A creator may edit their own content, but cannot access another creator's private analytics or financial records.
- Administrators may moderate any video, but sensitive financial actions should require elevated permissions and an audit record.
- Payout account changes should require re-authentication and, ideally, a verification process.
- Users must never be able to grant themselves creator or administrator status by editing a request in the browser.
- Support staff, if added later, should have restricted permissions rather than full administrator access.
