Backend modules
Keep these responsibilities in separate modules even if they run in one Express application.
Module	Responsibility
auth	Login, registration, sessions, password resets and account verification
users	Viewer profiles, settings and account management
creators	Applications, approvals, profiles and payout onboarding
videos	Metadata, categories, pricing, publishing and moderation status
uploads	Secure upload sessions, file validation and processing jobs
streaming	Entitlement checks, playback authorization and signed access
payments	Checkout, callbacks, transaction verification and refunds
purchases	Orders, purchase history and unique ownership records
ledger	Commission calculations, financial postings and adjustments
payouts	Creator balances, payout requests and settlement tracking
discovery	Search, recommendations, trending content and feeds
engagement	Comments, likes, ratings, follows and watch history
moderation	Reports, copyright claims, review queues and takedowns
notifications	Email, in-app notifications and payment updates
admin	User management, system configuration and privileged actions
audit	Security logs, admin activity and financial-operation history

Use background workers for transcoding, thumbnail generation, notifications, analytics aggregation and retryable operations. Critical payment processing and entitlement grants must be durable, transactional and idempotent.
9. Complete MySQL database design
Use MySQL with InnoDB, foreign keys, indexes, UTC timestamps and monetary values stored as integer minor units or exact decimal values. For RWF, store whole-franc amounts as integers if the business rules do not require fractional francs. Never use floating-point types for money.

The following schema is a practical production-oriented starting point. It includes the primary marketplace, access control, creator earnings, payment processing, video delivery, engagement and administration.
A. Accounts, roles and creators

CREATE TABLE users (
    id BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    public_id CHAR(36) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    email VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    phone VARCHAR(32) NULL UNIQUE,
    password_hash VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    display_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    avatar_url VARCHAR(2048) NULL,
    status ENUM('active','suspended','banned','pending_verification')
        NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending_verification',
    email_verified_at DATETIME NULL,
    phone_verified_at DATETIME NULL,
    last_login_at DATETIME NULL,
    created_at DATETIME NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    updated_at DATETIME NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
        ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
) ENGINE=InnoDB;

CREATE TABLE roles (
    id SMALLINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    name VARCHAR(40) NOT NULL UNIQUE
);

CREATE TABLE user_roles (
    user_id BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
    role_id SMALLINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
    assigned_by BIGINT UNSIGNED NULL,
