CREATE TABLE payout_allocations (
    payout_id BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
    earning_id BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
    allocated_amount BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
    PRIMARY KEY (payout_id, earning_id),
    FOREIGN KEY (payout_id) REFERENCES payouts(id),
    FOREIGN KEY (earning_id) REFERENCES creator_earnings(id)
) ENGINE=InnoDB;



The commission rate is stored in basis points: 2000 represents 20%. Calculate commission using integer arithmetic with a documented rounding rule. Save the rate used for each sale so that future changes to commission rules do not rewrite historical transactions.

The schema above is a foundation, not the entire production migration set. Before launch, also implement financial ledger entries, refunds, webhook deduplication, user sessions, notifications, watch history, follows, comments, likes, ratings, reports, audit logs and upload sessions.
